# Everything that is not Xcode's build output lives here; pet-app/.gitignore
# holds only what the project generates. One rule per thing, in one place --
# the two files used to repeat each other, and a pattern with a slash in it is
# anchored to the file it is written in, so the copies did not even mean the
# same thing.

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Local secrets and logs
.env
*.log

# Local debug/scratch output, never intentional to commit
tmp-screenshots/

# Working notes, kept on disk and out of the repository. None of them tell
# somebody who cloned this anything they can use: a task list with commit
# hashes in it, a release checklist, why decisions that predate this
# repository were taken, and a design-token table whose source of truth is
# ClientPalette/ClientTheme anyway. The README is what an outside reader
# gets.
docs/
pet-app/design.md

# AI-generated planning/analysis/design docs, same reasoning as above.
.superpowers/

# Isolated workspaces for subagent-driven development
.worktrees/

# graphify knowledge graph output
graphify-out/

CLAUDE.md
